WF-31 — Payment Submitted Handler

## Summary

- Inputs: phoneNumber, userId, messageText, messageContent, userStatus, user.name (from caller WF-01 for payment_submitted users)
- Outputs: WhatsApp "under review" reassurance to user AND a Slack relay of the user message into the user's consult channel; or hand-off to WF-47
- State Transitions: none (stop_intent path delegates to WF-47)
- Calls Sub-Workflows: WF-25 (Intent Classifier), WF-47 (Unsubscribe), WF-50 (Send WhatsApp), WF-51 (Send Slack)
- **Ambiguities / Notes:**
  - The trigger fans out into two parallel branches: an intent-classification branch and an unconditional Slack-relay branch. The Slack relay therefore fires for every inbound message in `payment_submitted` state — including `stop_intent` and `garbage` — independently of the intent path.

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — Triggered by parent with {phoneNumber, userId, messageText, messageContent, userStatus, user}.
Step 2: Fan out in parallel from trigger:
  - Branch A → Step 3 (intent classification + user reply)
  - Branch B → Step 9 (admin Slack relay)

(Branch A — user reply)
Step 3: Call WF-25 with phoneNumber, userId, messageText, userStatus. Receive intentResult.
Step 4: Check: Is intentResult NOT one of {garbage, malicious_abusive, inappropriate, stop_intent}?
  - If YES → go to Step 5
  - If NO → go to Step 7
Step 5: Build "under review" message: "⏳ Your payment is currently under review. Chinmay will verify it and get back to you shortly (usually within a few hours). You don't need to do anything else right now. If you have any questions, feel free to ask!"
Step 6: Call WF-50 with phoneNumber and the message. Go to Step 12.
Step 7: Check: Is intentResult == "stop_intent"?
  - If YES → go to Step 8
  - If NO → go to Step 12 (silently drop garbage/abusive/inappropriate)
Step 8: Call WF-47 (Unsubscribe) with phoneNumber, userId, userStatus. Go to Step 12.

(Branch B — relay user message into Slack consult channel)
Step 9: SELECT slack_channel_id FROM chinmay_astro.users WHERE phone_number = phoneNumber LIMIT 1.
Step 10: Build relay payload: channelId = slack_channel_id; messageText = "💬 Message from <user.name or phoneNumber> (payment under review):\n><messageContent>".
Step 11: Call WF-51 (Send Slack) with the payload.
Step 12: End.
